{
  "description": "The merchant's Bitcoin node (SPEC.md §31, The merchant's Bitcoin node; SPEC.md §30, The record). `urls`: each text (`url`) and, when it is a node URL, where the node is read (`expected`: `rest`, the `<explorer>` of SPEC.md §31 Explorers, and `webSocket`), else null. `channels`: the channel's `bitcoinNode` as written (`value`; absent: the field is absent) and the node it gives (`expected`: its `url`, `fallback` and `payers`), or null when there is none (the server reads mempool.space), the channel valid either way. `reads`: one read of the explorer (a REST read; the two reads of a check's step 1, an address's transactions and the chain's height, which are one read and fail when either fails; or a WebSocket's connection, which fails when it fails or is lost before any message): the node (`node`: its `fallback`, whether it failed a read less than 60 s ago in the same call (`failedRecently`) and whether it answers this read (`answers`); null: none), whether mempool.space answers it (`mempoolAnswers`); `expected`: the explorers asked, in order (`asked`), and whose answer the read gives (`result`: `node`, `mempool`, or `network` when it fails); it holds for a checkout link's page too, with the node of the link's record. A node that failed less than 60 s ago is asked after mempool.space as a server SHOULD ask it (SPEC.md §31): a port that does not follow that advice checks only the cases whose `failedRecently` is false. `records`: a checkout link's record value, opened, valid in every case (SPEC.md §30, Reading a record: the cases of `records` of checkout-links.json with a `bitcoinNode` added), and the node its page reads (`expected`: its `url` and `fallback`), or null for mempool.space (no `bitcoinNode`, one set aside, or a record of version 1, which ignores it). `writes`: the channel's `bitcoinNode` that `createInvoice` read (`channel`; absent: the field is absent) and whether the order has an address (`address`: a record of version 2, else of version 1), and the `bitcoinNode` its checkout link's record holds (`expected`), or null when the record has none (the field absent).",
